{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1468541-a-changeling-and-scion-mix","id":1468541,"title":"A changeling and scion mix","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-21T18:05:22-08:00","id":1468541,"title":"A changeling and scion mix","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A changeling and scion mix. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hi everybody! So! If you are unaware, in both editions of Changeling: The Lost, fae player characters can make a contract ,a Bargain ,with literally anything, be it abstract or concrete. Examples include a contract with the tides,and with the Confucian principle of companionship.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This last one inspired me to make a group of changelings that made a Bargain with a deity from classical mythology. I confess I'm not super sure how those can exist in the Chronicles of Darkness,but honestly? If you can make the Bargain with a Confucianist principle,a God it's not too far fetched. Some say Confucius is a God after all. As to build hype for Kith and Kin and Scion:God (both upcoming products by Onyx Path Publishing) I picked the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Ilhim. </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">canannite Gods. They are set to show up in Scion:God.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lost Dynasty: The Baal</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Most changelings were slaves,one way or another, that's perhaps the saddest fact of their lives. Even after escaping, many struggle to regain a sense of hope. Because from their point of view, their enslavers seemed to be gods.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What if then, they met </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>real</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> gods. Truly numinous beings? Beings that literally hung the moon and sun in the sky?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suppose then,that for their own reasons those deities are A-Ok with Bargaining with the scions?</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Baal,or the Lord's are what you get from that. The Changelings from ancient canaan didn't let the true Fae break their spirits, they found the great gods of their lands</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It is said the Bargain was simple,the Gods would grant the Lost a Mantle of Power if they pointed the way to Arcadia, for Hammon and his kin were hungry for conquest. The Bargain was struck</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some even say they acted as charioteers for those deities in a siege on Arcadia itself. No one knows if they succeeded</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In modern age,the Ba'al are open for any changeling who chooses to convert to the Ilhim religion. After proving their loyalty,they receive their first mantle dot and their story is forever bound with the Gods.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mantle of the Baal (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Their Mien become hot and dry like the desert, they eye colors are reddened ever so slowly, the sounds of clashing blades are heard in the distance\u2026.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 Gain bonus dice equal to your character\u2019s Mantle on physical rolls to defeat an enemy in a strategic manner. this means you have to plan the attack,it can\u2019t be mindless.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022 Gain bonus dice equal to your character\u2019s Mantle on mundane rolls to directly build something physical and concrete</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain three dots of the Fast Reflexes merit (changeling p. 123)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain two willpower points every time making a sacrifice to the gods cause you a major setback</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 spend 1 willpower point to inflict the Demoralized Condition on a enemy with a touch;</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Contracts.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Love and War (Commonl)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The changeling prays to Astarte: goddess of love and war for 7 minutes and it can make people either aggressive or lustful</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2 Glamour + 1 Willpower</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: Presence + Occult + Mantle vs Opponent\u2019s Willpower</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Action: Instant (takes 7 m inutes)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Roll Results</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success: The victim gains a condition representing their new lustful or angry state,it lasts a scene</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success: The Condition lasts for 48 hours</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure: The Contract fails.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure: The changeling takes 1 lethal damage,due to the prayers not being enough.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I\u2019ll Play King, You\u2019ll Play Soldier.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If a loyal friend or servant of the changeling is defending him,he can make them stronger.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2 Glamour + 1 Willpower</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool: Resolve + Occult + Mantle</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success: The subject gains 9-again quality on rolls to defend the scion</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Sucess: The subject gains the 8 again quality instead.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure, The Contract fails.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure: the changeling can\u2019t use the contract for 96 hours.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 11-21-2021, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T18:09:24-08:00","id":1468542,"title":"","content":"if you enjoyed this and wanted me to do another pantheon here's the poll<br /> <br /> A)Hindu Gods<br /> B:Oibway Gods<br /> C)Irish Gods<br /> D)Incan Gods","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T18:42:15-08:00","id":1468544,"title":"","content":"My interpretation of CoD is that except for the gods of Mummy: the Curse there are no true gods in the CoD. This is in contrast to the WoD, which does have real gods. However, in Dark Eras II there is canon support for the idea of True Fae impersonating Greek gods. There\u2019s no reason they couldn\u2019t do that for other pantheons, which could explain the Bargains your characters struck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T19:02:19-08:00","id":1468545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1468541-a-changeling-and-scion-mix?p=1468544#post1468544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My interpretation of CoD is that except for the gods of Mummy: the Curse there are no true gods in the CoD. This is in contrast to the WoD, which does have real gods. However, in Dark Eras II there is canon support for the idea of True Fae impersonating Greek gods. There\u2019s no reason they couldn\u2019t do that for other pantheons, which could explain the Bargains your characters struck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no,the cofd has plenty of gods,astral gods,supernal gods,shadow gods,pangaeans... Any of them could be the Ilhim","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T19:15:30-08:00","id":1468546,"title":"","content":"Even better; the gods being bargained with here needn\u2019t even exist \u2018for real\u2019 \u2014 it\u2019s all a contract after all, and contracts can be made with \u2018legal persons\u2019\u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> A. for the vote, because while the other three are more interesting, A is the only one I\u2019d know enough to actually recognize when I see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T19:18:05-08:00","id":1468547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1468541-a-changeling-and-scion-mix?p=1468546#post1468546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even better; the gods being bargained with here needn\u2019t even exist \u2018for real\u2019 \u2014 it\u2019s all a contract after all, and contracts can be made with \u2018legal persons\u2019\u2026\u2026<br /> <br /> A. for the vote, because while the other three are more interesting, A is the only one I\u2019d know enough to actually recognize when I see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>duly noted <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T22:53:26-08:00","id":1468568,"title":"","content":"I would really enjoy the C pantheon option","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T07:49:19-08:00","id":1468687,"title":"","content":"C for Irish Gods would be great. They already are so tied to the legends of the Fae, the interplay would be great","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby